<title>SINGAPORE: India offers to sell 25,000/T Bombay Nov naphtha.</title>
<headline>India offers to sell 25,000/T Bombay Nov naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) is selling by tender 25,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting November 14-16, industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender which closes October 31 and is valid until November 1, is offering the cargo from Bombay, on the west coast.</p>
<p>IOC's last Bombay HAN tender for a cargo lifting October 17-19 was awarded at $25.55 per tonne below Northwest European spot prices, on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
